  "compatibility_gaps": [
    "API-005 and API-006 use binary serialization (BinaryFormatter) via eShopLegacy.Utilities.Serializing which is deprecated and insecure in modern .NET; legacy and ported apps should migrate to JSON or other safe serialization",
    "API-001/API-002 (Brands GET) return identical CatalogBrand collections but legacy uses Web API 2 IEnumerable while ported uses ASP.NET Core Ok(); no functional incompatibility but serialization libraries (Newtonsoft.Json 12.0.1 vs 13.0.2) differ",
    "eShopLegacyMVC uses EF6 (manual HiLo ID generation via raw SQL) while eShopPorted uses EF Core 2.2 (identity columns); ID generation strategies diverge, complicating cross-application data synchronization"
  ],
  "unresolved_questions": [
    "Exact UseMockData and UseCustomizationData configuration logic in eShopPorted/appsettings.json is not wired; unclear which ICatalogService implementation (real vs mock) is registered at runtime",
    "eShopPorted still targets net461 despite ASP.NET Core 2.2 packages; unclear if this is intentional or incomplete migration; runtime compatibility not verified",
    "No authentication or authorization decorators ([Authorize], [AllowAnonymous]) visible on any API contracts; security posture unclear",
    "PictureFileName mapping and physical file path resolution differ: legacy uses Server.MapPath(\"~/Pics\"), ported uses empty string; file serving behavior may diverge"
  ],
